  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Svenskt program f&#xf6;r Kenyas f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade handelsmilj&#xf6; och inkludering (KETEI)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Swedish Program for Kenya&apos;s Enhanced Trade Environment and Inclusion (KETEI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A trade and development programme aimed at enhancing Kenya&apos;s national objectives in greening of border markets and infrastructure, development of climate-trade related regulatory frameworks, enhanced resilience of women and youth owned SME participation in trade and enhanced port competitiveness.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Ett handels- och utvecklingsprogram som syftar till att st&#xe4;rka Kenyas nationella m&#xe5;l f&#xf6;r gr&#xf6;nare gr&#xe4;nsmarknader och infrastruktur, utveckling av klimatrelaterade regelverk f&#xf6;r handel, &#xf6;kad motst&#xe5;ndskraft f&#xf6;r kvinnors och ungdomars deltagande i handel genom sm&#xe5; och medelstora f&#xf6;retag samt f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad hamnkonkurrenskraft</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Swedish Program for Kenya&apos;s Enhanced Trade Environment and Inclusion (KETEI) is designed to address critical policy, inclusion and environmental challenges in Kenya&apos;s trade arena. The goal of the program is: To promote inclusive and sustainable economic development in Kenya through increased green and inclusive export trade.  

By the end of the program, KETEI is expected to contribute to the following specific objectives: 

&#x2022; Enhanced port performance? through improved operations efficiency through installation of smart gates solution through implementing a smart gate solution at Mombasa Port and Naivasha Inland Container Depot (ICD) and build a body of knowledge from the feasibility study for greening Mombasa Port and the Naivasha Dry Port that will examine e-mobility options to reduce emissions and enhance sustainability in port operations. 
&#x2022; Promote trade inclusivity in Kenya. Through enhancing market access for SMEs especially those owned by women, youth and people with disabilities. 
&#x2022; Establish strong connections between local SMEs and international buyers, creating sustainable linkages that enhance market access.</narrative>
  </description>
